@startuml uc_sprint5
' NOTE: this source is no longer what the report prints. GraphViz routes
' every edge itself, so an actor's association came out curved, or under
' linetype polyline as straight segments with a corner in them. The figure
' is now laid out by hand and generated by docs/figures/gen_drawio_usecase.py.
' Kept as the readable model of the diagram: change both, or they drift.
title Sprint 5 — Agile planning

left to right direction

skinparam linetype polyline

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam actorBorderColor #808080
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #808080
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam TitleFontSize 13
skinparam TitleFontColor #333333

actor "Director\n(DIRECTEUR)"          as Dir
actor "Project Manager\n(CHEF_PROJET)" as PM
actor "Developer\n(DEVELOPPEUR)"       as Dev

rectangle "PMS Platform" {
  usecase "Create an\niteration" as UC1
  usecase "Maintain a prioritised\nproduct backlog" as UC2
  usecase "Commit an item\nto an iteration" as UC3
  usecase "Follow progress\non the board" as UC4
  usecase "Authenticate" as UC0
}

PM -- UC1
PM -- UC2
PM -- UC3
PM -- UC4
Dir -- UC4
Dev -- UC4
UC1 ..> UC0 : <<include>>
UC2 ..> UC0 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> UC0 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> UC0 : <<include>>

note right of UC2
  An item with no iteration stays in the product
  backlog: not committed is a normal state.
end note

@enduml
